feat(conversions): GET /conversions paginated, filtered history

What: Adds the GET /conversions endpoint returning a paginated conversion history
filtered by transactionId, date (whole UTC day) and/or clientId (at least one
required, else 400 CONVERSION_FILTER_REQUIRED). Query composed via
JpaSpecificationExecutor with per-filter Specification factories, @EntityGraph
fetch of the client association, stable createdAt DESC/id DESC sort, and a
dedicated response envelope (no Spring Page on the wire). Conversion domain
record gains clientId; POST /conversions wire format unchanged.
Why: Closes REQ-3 (.claude/Java-Assignment.pdf — GET /conversions?transactionId=
&date=&clientId=&page=&size=), the last unclosed endpoint requirement.
Tested: ConversionHistoryIntegrationTest (17 full-stack cases incl. UTC-day
boundary, AND-combined filters, empty-match, paging bounds/defaults/stability,
malformed and non-numeric inputs), ConversionServiceTest, ConversionControllerTest,
ForeignExchangeControllerAdviceTest, mapper tests. Full suite 158/158,
checkstyle 0 violations.

